# What `.map` Really Means

`.map` basically means:

```text id="xmlns204"
“Take each item, transform it somehow, and return a NEW collection.”
```

---

# Simple Example

```ruby id="xmlns205"
numbers = [1, 2, 3]

numbers.map { |number| number * 3 }
```

Result:

```text id="xmlns206"
[3, 6, 9]
```

Ruby:

1. grabs each number
2. transforms it
3. builds a NEW array automatically

