# Cleaner `.map` Usage

You wrote:

```ruby id="xmlns225"
persons.map {|person| persons_name << person[:name]}
```

This works…

BUT cleaner `.map` style would be:

```ruby id="xmlns226"
persons_name = persons.map { |person| person[:name] }
```

Why?

Because `.map` automatically builds the new array for you.

That’s one of the major benefits of `.map`.

